 ## [Unreleased]
 
+### New features
+
+- The Telsiz DJ player can be moved: when the DJ card is not visible, the player in the corner of the screen can be dragged by its bar and dropped in one of the four corners, the Move button goes through the corners in turn, and the chosen corner is stored on the device. Between 760 and 1279 pixels the player sits at the top right below the band by default, and in a bottom corner it moves above the message box and the radio card as long as there is room, so it does not cover the voice buttons. Minimize leaves only the bar: an audio file keeps playing, and a YouTube track pauses on that device only and resumes in sync with the room with Show. The Floating Player switch keeps the player in the corner even while the card is visible, and an audio file then also shows in the corner with its waveform and bar. The name of the playing track and "Telsiz DJ · room" appear in your system's media controls and on the lock screen, which can be turned off in the Media controls section of Settings > Privacy. Play and Pause there only affect that device and do not stop the room's music. When someone else adds a track to Telsiz DJ in your voice room, a line with the track's name appears in the Notifications list.
+
 ### Changes
 
 - The placeholder of the Add Friend field now reads "Enter a username" (before "username"). The field's label is only visible to screen readers, so the placeholder is the only visible hint.
 - The desktop app tells the page the window state and the system idle time. The page learns through `telsizDesktop.onWindowState` when the window is minimized, comes back from being minimized (including going back to full screen), is hidden to the tray and is shown again (including coming back from the tray). It reads the time since the last user input in whole seconds through `telsizDesktop.idleSeconds()`, and the background windows of frequencies that are not open read it through `telsizArkaPlan.idleSeconds()`. Only one of four state values reaches the page, and only the app window and background windows may read the idle time. These channels are the desktop groundwork for Telsiz DJ, the floating window and automatic idle, and make no visible change on their own.
+- In Telsiz DJ a new track, a track change and resuming are anchored 3 seconds ahead for YouTube tracks and 1.5 seconds ahead for audio files (before, every track was anchored 1.5 seconds ahead and resuming happened at once). Devices load during this time and start together from the same point. While a YouTube track is playing in the room, a person who has not allowed the YouTube player yet sees a notice with Load the YouTube Player and No, Don't Load It buttons on the radio card, and a short notification appears for every new YouTube track even while the DJ card is open. In the desktop app, a YouTube track pauses on this device when the window is minimized or hidden in the tray and resumes in sync with the room when the window comes back. Audio files play in a single audio element. While the DJ column is open, the stage layout is built with flexbox instead of a grid (it looks the same).
 
 ### Fixes
 
+- Telsiz DJ: the first YouTube track added while the tab was in the background (or the desktop window was minimized) never started on that device and started in the middle once the page came to the front. The card is now drawn on a hidden page too, and the track starts together with the other devices. The announcement in the text room did not show the track's name ("added a YouTube track"), and now it goes out with the name: the name is awaited for up to 8 seconds, if it arrives later the announcement of the person who added it is edited with the name, and the edited label is not shown. A file added with "Play in DJ" was never announced, and now it is announced with its name in the text room where the file is. The last action line on the DJ card also reads the name from the queue. In windows narrower than 1280 pixels the player in the corner covered the voice buttons of the radio card.
 - In the Arcade and Turquoise and Copper themes the border of the camera indicator on the radio card ("Your camera is on, everyone in the room can see it") and of the notice shown when someone starts sharing their screen was not drawn at all. The muted Microphone and active Camera buttons of a direct message call, the chip and panel of your own share, the Stop Watching button, the Telsiz DJ error box and the verified safety number button were also drawn in the text color instead of their own border color. Both themes now have live and danger border colors, and the borders show with at least 3:1 contrast on every surface.
 
